{
  "methodology_note": "Every metrics block is reported under TWO detection definitions: 'production_flag_only' (Layer 3.3's classify_days() flag_type -- overclaim/night-injection/stuck-sensor -- what the dashboard and evidence bundles actually use) and 'including_cusum' (also counts CUSUM's own day-level flag, which is architecturally SEPARATE from classify_days() -- conformal.py never consults it -- but is Overview v2 SS3.5's stated intended mechanism for A6_slow_drift specifically; reporting only the production flag would silently understate A6 recall). A day is 'detected' if flagged by ANY counted mechanism, regardless of whether that mechanism 'matches' the injected anomaly. Per-type recall is independently well-defined; per-type precision reuses a SHARED clean+hard-negative false-positive pool across all types (false positives have no injected type of their own) -- read precision_i as 'precision vs. non-fraud days for this type specifically', not a fully independent per-type statistic. AUC-PR ranks by severity_kwh (flag-type-aware magnitude, unaffected by the CUSUM question) against binary is_positive labels.",
